course: dictionary
lesson: 377
title: Anxious: worried or keen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Anxious» means worried or nervous about something that might happen. «She was anxious about the test» tells you she was worried it might go wrong. Look for clue words near it, such as about, worry or fear.
explain: The same word can mean something different. «He was anxious to help» means he wanted to help very much. The clue is «to help»: you are not worried about helping, you are keen to do it. Try both meanings in the sentence and see which one fits.
explain: Writers use clues to show that a character is anxious. A character who bites her nails, cannot sleep or keeps checking things is anxious, because she fears something will go wrong. Feeling anxious sometimes is normal, and it helps to talk to a trusted grown-up.
fact: «Anxious» means worried or nervous about something that might happen.
fact: «Anxious» can also mean wanting something very much, as in «anxious to help».
fact: Common phrases with anxious are anxious about, anxious for, anxious to, and an anxious wait.
fact: «Clingy» means anxious and unwilling to leave the parent.
fact: Feeling anxious sometimes is normal, and it helps to talk to a trusted grown-up.
exercise: «The new girl was anxious about her first day at school.» What does anxious mean here? | Bored and tired | Angry with the teacher | Eager to get to school very quickly | *Worried that something might go wrong
exercise: «He was anxious to help his gran carry the shopping.» What does anxious mean here? | Worried that he might drop the shopping | *Wanting to help very much | Too tired to move | Angry at his gran
exercise: Find and copy the word that shows someone is worried in this sentence: «Teasing about how someone looks can make them anxious and lonely for years.» | lonely | years | *anxious | teasing
test: A child who holds tightly to her mum at the school gate and will not let go is best described as what? | Bold | Cheerful | Sleepy | *Clingy
test: Jayden says «anxious» is just a fancy word for angry. Why is he wrong? | Anxious means happy and calm | Anxious means angry, but only at night | *Anxious means worried or nervous, not angry | He is right, they mean the same
exam: Which sentence uses anxious to mean wanting something very much? | Dad was anxious about the storm | She sat through an anxious wait by the phone | *They were anxious to start the game | Mum felt anxious during the test
